N:HOW READ (2026-11-10): read from the BBM/USP plate at 220 dpi and enlarged crops. The source marks 2/4 and crotchet 96, prints eight bars, and includes a written G-sharp. This first pass is deliberately left at transcription status rather than claiming a completed source check.
N:UNCERTAIN: every pitch and duration wants a second independent plate reading; the opening four notes, the pickup/rest placement in bars 2 and 4, the slurs in bars 2, 4 and 7, and whether the final note is accented.
N:Words preserve Andrade's 1928 spelling. Verses 2 and 3 are retained below rather than forced under the first verse's rhythm.
